  "fields": {
    "title": "Neomorphism",
    "textContent": {
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Description",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Neomorphism or Neumorphism refers to a trend that was primarily popular on ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "uri": "https://dribbble.com/search/neomorphism"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "Dribbble",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": " in 2020. Neomorphism can be characterized by a soft and light look. Elements are usually the same color as the background and are only distinguished by shadows and highlights surrounding the element. In this way, Neomorphism suggested a certain multidimensionality and haptics, which can be described in most examples as pure visual gimmick without deeper meaning. Due to a lack of ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "4TzAZFehkMPRfclxZU7jhz",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "accessibility",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": " for people with visual impairments and non demonstrable advantages, apart from a visual language that differs from the standard, this design trend disappeared again quite quickly.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {
            "target": {
              "sys": {
                "id": "2ptFRbXnDoJ8YALGlGwwSN",
                "type": "Link",
                "linkType": "Asset"
              }
            }
          },
          "content": [],
          "nodeType": "embedded-asset-block"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "value": "Skeumorphism (left), Flat design (middle) and Neomorphism (right) in comparison",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Background",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "The term Neomorphism was coined by Jason Kelly to describe the Combination of the widespread ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "2ZTXtv3YeWVkbsEYoZWnez",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "flat ",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "aesthetics of modern interface elements with the three-dimensional look of the first websites of the 90s and 00s, also known as ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "2Ib0yeXE5iLTu4gX6TDg0e",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "Skeuomorphism",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": ". In 2020, Apple released macOS Big Sur, which included Elements in neumorph style, like app icons.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "nodeType": "document"
    },
